{
  "answer": "To use lifespan events to initialize and clean up shared resources in FastAPI, you can define event handlers (functions) that need to be executed before the application starts up, or when the application is shutting down. These functions can be declared with `async def` or normal `def`. You can use the `lifespan` parameter of the `FastAPI` app to define these event handlers. This approach is recommended over the deprecated `startup` and `shutdown` events. For more details, you can refer to the documentation at [Starlette's Lifespan' docs](https://starlette.dev/lifespan/). [advanced/events-9]",
